::ALG2_U01_L02_GuidedPractice_Q01::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Simplify (3x² + 2x - 5) + (x² - 7x + 9).
{
=A. 4x² - 5x + 4 #Correct. Combine like terms: 3x squared plus x squared is 4x squared, 2x minus 7x is -5x, and -5 plus 9 is 4.
~B. 4x² + 9x + 4 #This adds 2x and 7x instead of combining 2x and -7x.
~C. 3x⁴ - 5x + 4 #This incorrectly adds exponents when adding like terms. Exponents stay the same when like terms are combined.
~D. 4x² - 5x - 14 #This combines the variable terms correctly but multiplies the constants instead of adding them.
}

::ALG2_U01_L02_GuidedPractice_Q02::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_GP_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Simplify (5x² - 3x + 8) - (2x² + x - 6).
{
~A. 3x² - 2x + 2 #This does not distribute the subtraction sign to every term in the second polynomial.
~B. 7x² - 2x + 2 #This adds the x squared terms and does not subtract the second polynomial.
=C. 3x² - 4x + 14 #Correct. Distribute the subtraction sign to get 5x squared - 3x + 8 - 2x squared - x + 6, then combine like terms.
~D. 3x² + 4x + 14 #The x-term sign is incorrect. -3x - x equals -4x.
}

::ALG2_U01_L02_GuidedPractice_Q03::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_GP_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Simplify 3x(2x² - 5x + 4).
{
~A. 6x² - 15x + 12 #This multiplies coefficients but does not add exponents when multiplying by x.
=B. 6x³ - 15x² + 12x #Correct. Distribute 3x to each term and add exponents for powers with the same base.
~C. 6x³ - 5x² + 4x #This does not multiply every coefficient by 3.
~D. 6x³ + 15x² + 12x #The middle term should be negative because 3x times -5x is -15x squared.
}

::ALG2_U01_L02_GuidedPractice_Q04::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_GP_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
Simplify (x + 4)(x - 6).
{
~A. x² - 24 #This multiplies only the first and last terms and misses the middle products.
~B. x² + 10x - 24 #This uses +6x instead of -6x when multiplying x by -6.
~C. x² + 2x - 24 #The middle terms should combine to -2x, not +2x.
=D. x² - 2x - 24 #Correct. x squared - 6x + 4x - 24 combines to x squared - 2x - 24.
}

::ALG2_U01_L02_GuidedPractice_Q05::
Question ID: ALG2_U01_L02_GP_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.AE.2; MLA.A2.AE.4
Question:
A rectangle has length x + 3 and width x + 5. What polynomial represents the area?
{
~A. 2x + 8 #This adds length and width, but area requires multiplication.
=B. x² + 8x + 15 #Correct. Area is (x + 3)(x + 5), which equals x squared + 8x + 15.
~C. x² + 15 #This multiplies only the first and last terms and misses the middle terms.
~D. x² - 8x + 15 #The middle term should be positive because both binomial constants are positive.
}

